  "definitions": "Career-assistant (RAG) benchmark: routing, grounding and relevance, deterministic vs local LLM. Every metric is computed automatically from explicit definitions (no LLM judge): * routing accuracy routed intent == expected intent. * citation validity share of PROPOSED sentences (before the verifier) whose citations are non-empty and all refer to documents that were actually given. * faithfulness share of proposed sentences that pass the verifier: every skill, credential, number, proper noun and level word must occur in the cited documents, and the sentence must share content with them. hallucination rate = 1 - faithfulness (on proposed sentences). * residual unsupported sentences SHOWN to the user that fail the verifier: 0 by construction - the number that matters is how much the verifier had to remove (above), and the limits of what it can check (qualitative claims without entities), discussed in the report. * answer relevance cosine similarity (multilingual-e5) between the question and the final answer. * retrieval relevance for questions that name skills: share of cited listings that require ALL those skills. * safety share of final answers containing a probability / salary / hiring-guarantee claim. * latency wall-clock seconds per answer; LLM token volume estimated as characters / 4."
}
